      "severity": "concern",
      "claim": "The Context section states every line number in it was read at commit 958db033, but this spec's base is f24e3fb6, many commits later. Between those two commits saffron/cell/session.py changed by 257 lines, saffron/cli.py by 197, saffron/ledger.py by 148, saffron/phases/review.py by 19, tests/test_session.py by 1143, and tests/test_cli.py by 614, while saffron/task.py, saffron/phases/rebut.py, saffron/scheduler.py and tests/test_task.py did not change. Citations into the unchanged files are exact or within a line or two, but citations into the heavily-changed files drift badly: session.py:3159-3170 (the cell's final outcome write) is actually at 3243-3258; session.py:2711-2712 (the REVIEWING write) is actually 2788; session.py:3017-3018 (the REBUTTING write) is actually 3094; session.py:3010 (where review_state is read) is actually 3086; cli.py:1912 (reconcile's own call) is actually about 2093; cli.py:1885 and :1715 (the two stamp_orphaned=False callers) are actually about 1896 and 2066; cli.py:1628 (the batch's stamp_orphaned=True) is actually about 1809; ledger.py:768-775/776-790/1364-1367 (the two fact handlers and set_task_state's docstring) are actually about 810-816/818-830/1427-1430; test_session.py:2486 (the first broken test) is actually 2731, with its comparison lines nearer 2846-2850 than the cited 2602-2606; review.py:875 is actually 880. I verified the substance of every one of these claims is still true at the base despite the wrong line numbers, and no mutant or witness depends on a literal line offset (criterion 1's mutant matches on source text), so this does not break any criterion's build or witness. But a person skimming the Context section to sanity-check the spec before the cell starts would be looking at the wrong lines unless they re-derive each one themselves, as this review had to do.",
